---
layout: base.webc
title: Type specimen
description: Three typeface pairings shown at working sizes, for choosing between.
---
<div class="specimen">
  <header class="specimen__intro">
    <h1>Type specimen</h1>
    <p>
      Three pairings, each setting a work title beside a paragraph of running text
      at the sizes they would actually be used. Nothing on the rest of the site
      sets a <code>font-family</code>: once you have chosen, set
      <code>--font-display</code> and <code>--font-body</code> in
      <code>theme.css</code> and delete the two you did not pick.
    </p>
    <p class="specimen__note">
      All six faces are self-hosted and under the Open Font License. Redaction is
      the odd one out: it is not variable, and ships instead in seven grades of
      progressive degradation.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="pairing" aria-labelledby="pairing-a">
    <h2 class="pairing__label" id="pairing-a">A — Redaction &amp; Fraunces</h2>
    <div class="pairing__demo" style="--display: 'Redaction'; --body: 'Fraunces', 'Fraunces fallback', serif;">
      <div class="pairing__display">
        <p class="pairing__title">Untitled I</p>
        <p class="pairing__meta">2024 · oil on linen · 162 × 130 cm</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pairing__body">
        <p>
          The paint is thin at the edges and heaped at the centre, so the canvas
          reads as a surface before it reads as a picture. Standing close, the
          weave shows through; at four metres it closes into a single field.
        </p>
        <p>
          Handling, weight, colour, scale — the vocabulary a catalogue entry needs,
          set at the size a catalogue entry is actually read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pairing" aria-labelledby="pairing-b">
    <h2 class="pairing__label" id="pairing-b">B — Bricolage Grotesque &amp; Literata</h2>
    <div class="pairing__demo" style="--display: 'Bricolage Grotesque'; --body: 'Literata', 'Literata fallback', serif;">
      <div class="pairing__display">
        <p class="pairing__title">Untitled I</p>
        <p class="pairing__meta">2024 · oil on linen · 162 × 130 cm</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pairing__body">
        <p>
          The paint is thin at the edges and heaped at the centre, so the canvas
          reads as a surface before it reads as a picture. Standing close, the
          weave shows through; at four metres it closes into a single field.
        </p>
        <p>
          Handling, weight, colour, scale — the vocabulary a catalogue entry needs,
          set at the size a catalogue entry is actually read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pairing" aria-labelledby="pairing-c">
    <h2 class="pairing__label" id="pairing-c">C — Bodoni Moda &amp; Source Serif 4</h2>
    <div class="pairing__demo" style="--display: 'Bodoni Moda'; --body: 'Source Serif 4', 'Source Serif 4 fallback', serif;">
      <div class="pairing__display">
        <p class="pairing__title">Untitled I</p>
        <p class="pairing__meta">2024 · oil on linen · 162 × 130 cm</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pairing__body">
        <p>
          The paint is thin at the edges and heaped at the centre, so the canvas
          reads as a surface before it reads as a picture. Standing close, the
          weave shows through; at four metres it closes into a single field.
        </p>
        <p>
          Handling, weight, colour, scale — the vocabulary a catalogue entry needs,
          set at the size a catalogue entry is actually read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pairing" aria-labelledby="pairing-grades">
    <h2 class="pairing__label" id="pairing-grades">Redaction, on its own terms</h2>
    <p class="specimen__note">
      Only the undegraded cut is bundled. The other six grades are separate files;
      if the degradation is the reason to choose it, they are worth downloading.
    </p>
    <p class="pairing__title" style="--display: 'Redaction';">Debí tirar más fotos</p>
  </section>
</div>

<style webc:scoped>
  /*
    PROVISIONAL — this page is a measuring instrument, not a designed page. It
    sets sizes only so the comparison is fair, and deliberately makes no other
    choices. Delete the whole page once you have picked a pairing.
  */
  .specimen {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding-block: 2rem;
  }

  .specimen__intro {
    max-inline-size: 42rem;
  }

  .specimen__note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .pairing {
    border-block-start: 1px solid currentColor;
    padding-block-start: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pairing__label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.6;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  /* Title beside paragraph, so the two faces are judged in relation rather than
     one after the other. Stacks when there is not room for both. */
  .pairing__demo {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .pairing__demo {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 3fr);
    }
  }

  .pairing__title {
    font-family: var(--display), serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pairing__meta {
    font-family: var(--body), serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-block: 0.75rem 0;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .pairing__body {
    font-family: var(--body), serif;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-inline-size: 38rem;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .pairing__body p {
    margin-block: 0 1rem;
  }
</style>
